{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"The baseline reproduction confirms the controllable 5×5 color-9 avatar: actions 2 and 3 translate it down and left, blocked moves do nothing, while the color-14 mover advances only when movement succeeds. The goal-colored region lies above separated barriers, so helper progress and gate opening are the useful dense signals—not raw frame-change count. Next I’m testing the preserved contextual-commit beam itself, with its existing bounds, to see exactly where it stalls."}}
